{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25598404",
      "title": "Managing the User Input State",
      "sourceHash": "18460726958ab3d204210de5c91ec616c7bf26988656767576a0d2992ba83529",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 3.74,
          "en": "Lets continue with this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.74,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "And let's make sure we actually fetch user input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 8.69,
          "en": "so that we can then, in the next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.69,
          "end": 11.98,
          "en": "also render it as part of a list of users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.98,
          "end": 13.77,
          "en": "We got our AddUser Component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.77,
          "end": 15.967,
          "en": "with the addUserHandler, which is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.967,
          "end": 17.96,
          "en": "when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.96,
          "end": 22.12,
          "en": "And now the goal is to collect the two entered values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.12,
          "end": 24.06,
          "en": "the username and the age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.06,
          "end": 26.06,
          "en": "And utilize them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.06,
          "end": 29.07,
          "en": "Now to collect the values, we can use a technique",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.07,
          "end": 31.79,
          "en": "we already learned about in the last modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 31.79,
          "end": 34.478,
          "en": "We can use State Management in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.478,
          "end": 37.71,
          "en": "to update the state with every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.71,
          "end": 40.318,
          "en": "and hence save what the user enters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.318,
          "end": 42.91,
          "en": "in such a state variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.91,
          "end": 45.42,
          "en": "Which is then managed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 45.42,
          "end": 48.67,
          "en": "For that, we need to import the useState hook here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 48.67,
          "end": 50.55,
          "en": "inside of the AddUser Component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.55,
          "end": 52.283,
          "en": "And then we need to initialize it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.283,
          "end": 55.81,
          "en": "For that, we call useState and we can define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.81,
          "end": 58.393,
          "en": "the default, the initial starting state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.35,
          "end": 61.81,
          "en": "And since I want to manage one piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.81,
          "end": 63.97,
          "en": "for every input, the starting state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.97,
          "end": 66.207,
          "en": "will basically be, no input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.207,
          "end": 68.52,
          "en": "So an empty string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.52,
          "end": 73.42,
          "en": "And then I have my enteredUsername here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 73.42,
          "end": 77.15,
          "en": "And my state updating function, setEnteredUsername.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 79.57,
          "end": 81.794,
          "en": "Now, in case you're not sure what this syntax means,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 81.794,
          "end": 84.46000000000001,
          "en": "make sure you go through the respective lectures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 84.46000000000001,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "in the basics module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 87.87,
          "en": "This is a JavaScript syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 87.87,
          "end": 90.15,
          "en": "which is called array de-structuring",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 90.15,
          "end": 92.78999999999999,
          "en": "and we use it, because useState always",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 92.78999999999999,
          "end": 95.5,
          "en": "returns an array with exactly two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 95.5,
          "end": 97.95,
          "en": "And with this syntax, we're pulling these elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.95,
          "end": 99.16,
          "en": "out of that returned array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.16,
          "end": 101.17,
          "en": "And we store them in separate constants,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.17,
          "end": 104.57,
          "en": "of the name enteredUsername and setEnteredUsername.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 104.57,
          "end": 107.07,
          "en": "And I chose those names for those constants,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.07,
          "end": 110.05,
          "en": "because the first element of that returned array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 110.05,
          "end": 111.8,
          "en": "is the current state snapshot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 111.8,
          "end": 114.37,
          "en": "And every time this Component re-renders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 114.37,
          "end": 116.49600000000001,
          "en": "which it, for example, does when the state is updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.49600000000001,
          "end": 120.437,
          "en": "this concept will hold the latest state snapshot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.437,
          "end": 123.34,
          "en": "and setEnteredUsername on the other hand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 123.34,
          "end": 125.07,
          "en": "holds a function which we can call,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 125.07,
          "end": 127.89,
          "en": "to change that state and to then trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 127.89,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "such a re-render cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.13,
          "en": "So now, we need a function which is triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 132.13,
          "end": 134.335,
          "en": "on every keystroke of that input here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 134.335,
          "end": 135.925,
          "en": "And for that, I'll have my",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 135.925,
          "end": 139.94,
          "en": "usernameChangeHandler function for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 139.94,
          "end": 142.06,
          "en": "where I get the event object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 142.06,
          "end": 145.01,
          "en": "because we'll listen to a default DOM event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 145.01,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "and such events will dispatch objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 149.872,
          "en": "with more information and we can bind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 149.872,
          "end": 153.264,
          "en": "this to input here, for the onChange prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 153.264,
          "end": 157.25,
          "en": "Which then will tie this to the change event listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 157.25,
          "end": 160.27,
          "en": "So here I pass my usernameChangeHandler",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 160.27,
          "end": 162.21,
          "en": "and therefore, this function will be triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 162.21,
          "end": 165.65,
          "en": "for every keystroke in the input element, down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 165.65,
          "end": 169.15,
          "en": "And now, here I will call setEnteredUsername",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 169.15,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "and I wanna set it to what the user currently entered.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.51,
          "en": "And we can get that entered value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 174.51,
          "end": 177.25,
          "en": "with the help of that event object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 177.25,
          "end": 179.23,
          "en": "Because there we can access the target of the event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 179.23,
          "end": 180.69,
          "en": "which is the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 180.69,
          "end": 183.03,
          "en": "And then the value property of that input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 183.03,
          "end": 184.893,
          "en": "to get the currently entered value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 186.28,
          "end": 188.67,
          "en": "Now I'll just copy that and repeat that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 188.67,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "to also have a ageChangeHandler,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 192.45,
          "en": "where I call setEnteredAge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 196.65,
          "end": 198.5,
          "en": "because that's the second piece of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 198.5,
          "end": 201.52,
          "en": "and I wanna manage, hence I'll duplicate this as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 201.52,
          "end": 203.92000000000002,
          "en": "And here I have my enteredAge and setEnteredAge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 208.55,
          "end": 210.74,
          "en": "And with that, we're updating the enteredAge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 210.74,
          "end": 211.8,
          "en": "on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 211.8,
          "end": 213.18,
          "en": "We of course, also need to make",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 215.016,
          "en": "the connection down there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 215.016,
          "end": 216.94299999999998,
          "en": "So ageChangeHandler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 219.6,
          "end": 223.87,
          "en": "And now we got both username and the age stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 223.87,
          "end": 226.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, in addUserHandler, we can therefore now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 226.57999999999998,
          "end": 230.5,
          "en": "console.log, enteredUsername and enteredAge,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 230.5,
          "end": 232.77,
          "en": "whoops and enteredAge.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 234.67000000000002,
          "end": 239.11,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 239.11,
          "end": 240.886,
          "en": "And if we now save everything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 240.886,
          "end": 243.56,
          "en": "we can go back, open up the Developer Tools here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 243.56,
          "end": 246.49,
          "en": "and go to the JavaScript console and maybe enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 246.49,
          "end": 248,
          "en": "Max here and 31.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 248,
          "end": 250.803,
          "en": "And if I click Add User, you see that output here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 254.71,
          "en": "Now at the moment, we can also submit an empty form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 254.71,
          "end": 257.16,
          "en": "like an empty age field, but that's something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 257.16,
          "end": 258.33,
          "en": "we'll fix later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 258.33,
          "end": 261.053,
          "en": "Generally fetching that data works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 261.93,
          "end": 263.981,
          "en": "Now as a next step, let's make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 263.981,
          "end": 266.14,
          "en": "that when we click Add User,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 266.14,
          "end": 268.42,
          "en": "we actually reset these inputs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 268.42,
          "end": 271.38,
          "en": "so that both input fields are empty again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 271.38,
          "end": 272.90999999999997,
          "en": "And let's make sure we also have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 272.90999999999997,
          "end": 275.74,
          "en": "some basic validation, which simply makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 275.74,
          "end": 277.677,
          "en": "that nothing happens, that we don't",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 277.677,
          "end": 280.13,
          "en": "print this information here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 280.13,
          "end": 282.43,
          "en": "If one of the two input fields is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 282.43,
          "end": 286.02,
          "en": "or if the age is smaller than one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 286.02,
          "end": 289.8,
          "en": "or if it's equal to zero, or smaller than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 289.8,
          "end": 292.34000000000003,
          "en": "So that's something you can try on your own next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 292.34000000000003,
          "end": 295.14300000000003,
          "en": "We'll do it together in the next lecture, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}